{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775333384-m8SMtMfqaok8o6WyhwdI","role":"assistant","created":1775333394,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to extract the total amount outstanding for Treasury Notes from each of these three documents:\n\n1. March 30, 1962 (Table 3 - Treasury Notes)\n2. March 29, 1963 (Table 3 - Treasury Notes)\n3. March 31, 1964 (Table 3 - Treasury Notes)\n\nLet me parse through these to find the total \"Amount outstanding (millions)\" for Treasury Notes in each case.\n\nFrom 1962 (page 75), Table 3 - Treasury Notes:\nThe amounts listed are in the first column. Let me count them:\n- $2,211 (4% 5/15/62-E)\n- 158 (4 8/15/62-B)\n- 7,325 (3-1/4 8/15/62-G)\n- 1,143 (3-3/4 11/15/62-C)\n- 6,082 (3-1/4 11/15/62-H)\n- 2,839 (2-5/8 2/15/63-A)\n- 3,642 (3-1/4 2/15/63-E)\n- 1,743 (4 5/15/63-B)\n- 5,047 (3-1/4 5/15/63-D)\n- 3,011 (4-7/8 11/15/63-C)\n- 4,933 (4-3/4 5/15/64-A)\n- 3,893 (3-3/4 5/15/64-D)\n- 2,316 (5 8/15/64-B)\n- 5,019 (3-3/4 8/15/64-E)\n- 4,195 (4-7/8 11/15/64-C)\n- 2,113 (4-5/8 5/15/65-A)\n\n\n- 4,454 (4 8/15/66-A)\n- 86 (1-1/2 4/1/62-EA)\n- 590 (1-1/2 10/1/62-EO)\n- 533 (1-1/2 4/1/63-EA)\n- 506 (1-1/2 10/1/63-EO)\n- 457 (1-1/2 4/1/64-EA)\n- 490 (1-1/2 10/1/64-EO)\n- 466 (1-1/2 4/1/65-EA)\n\nI notice these are additional Treasury Notes with varying interest rates and maturity dates. I'll continue adding up the total amounts to get a comprehensive view of the outstanding notes.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_b2a70e9a087f434fa2ca8d86","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1962_04.json | python3 -c \"\nimport json\nimport sys\n\ndata = json.load(sys.stdin)\n\n# Find the table with Treasury Notes - look for Table 3\nfor table in data.get('tables', []):\n    if table.get('title', '').startswith('Table 3') and 'Treasury Notes' in table.get('title', ''):\n        print('Found Table 3 for 1962')\n        # Get all rows and sum the amount outstanding\n        total = 0\n        for row in table.get('data', []):\n            # First column is Amount outstanding\n            amount = row[0]\n            if amount and amount != '-':\n                # Remove $ and commas, parse as float\n                val = float(amount.replace('$', '').replace(',', ''))\n                total += val\n                print(f'  {amount} -> {val}')\n        print(f'Total: {total}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
